t-matched focus tables plus BIOL/GEOSC 474 from the PDF's Astronomy list (present in every year checked, an HTML-vs-PDF rendering gap, not a per-year change). NUTR 175 is still unrenamed this year (becomes NUTR 175N starting 2024-25). MATH 21 added (Semester 3) for the same real, catalog-verified, non-year-versioned DS 200/STAT 184 prereq reason as every other year in this set, despite this edition's own printed table not showing it either. All Program Requirements totals confirmed directly against this edition's own Program Requirements table 0 (unchanged from 2022: General Education 45, Electives 0-9, Requirements for the Major 75-84). Also: this edition's own raw Suggested Academic Plan table has TWO \"General Education Course\" items in First Year Spring (row 4's Fall=GenEd/Spring=GenEd pairing plus row 5's Fall=PSU 17/Spring=GenEd pairing), summing to that semester's own printed 17-credit subtotal (MATH 141 4 + CMPSC 132 3 + DS 200 4 + GenEd 3 + GenEd 3 = 17) -- confirmed directly in the raw HTML table cells for this edition. DATSC-2026.json's own Semester 2 only lists ONE \"GEN ED\" slot (summing to 14, short of its own stated target_credits of \"17\") -- verified this is the same real gap in the live 2026-27 edition's own printed table, not specific to this year, so it's a pre-existing gap in the already-built 2026 file, out of scope for this file to fix. Added the second GEN ED slot here so this file's own Semester 2 matches this edition's own printed 17-credit subtotal exactly.",
